    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI derived the `locality` field on the owner GET/create response from the owner's city using the fixed table.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` (readOnly string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/Localities.java`** (new) \u2014 holds the fixed `Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD` table and a `localityFor(city)` method returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` (also for null/unknown cities).\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that populates `locality` via `Localities.localityFor(owner.getCity())`, matching the existing pattern used for `membershipTier`/`displayName`.\n\nThe derivation flows through the existing `RespondWithOwner` function (used by `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}`), so `$.locality` is `\"NSW\"` for Sydney and `\"UNKNOWN\"` for cities not in the table, satisfying both acceptance tests.",
